# Engine layer "sly-redhat": RedHatAI/Qwen3.8-27B-MXFP4 profiles on the SAME engine layer as sly-official (official
# single-R9700 recipe). Own dir so sly-official/ stays the Swift-1.5 heretic recipe (SRP, 2026-10-30); the
# engine flags are not copied -- sly-official/_engine.env stays their single source of truth. Only the image differs:
# RedHat runs Sly 1.9.1 since 2026-10-30 (Cactus fade+cap, template v22.5-sly2: older turns' reasoning not replayed;
# smoke test bench/runs/2026-10-30-1745-sly-1.9.1-smoke/). Heretic (sly-official) stays on 1.8.1 until it is tested on 1.9.1.
# Rollback to 1.8.1 (image + its compile cache are kept): IMAGE=ghcr.io/slybase/vllm-sly-radiance:1.8.1-rocm10.1, or
# change the line below. 1.8.1-like Cactus on 1.9.1 instead: RADIANCE_CACTUS_FADE_END=0 + RADIANCE_CACTUS_CAP_R=0 in ENGINE_ENV.
IMAGE=${IMAGE:-ghcr.io/slybase/vllm-sly-radiance:1.9.1-rocm10.1}
source "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../sly-official/_engine.env"
